Z||000012||85blackgt||07-03-2001||11:08 AM||||hi cliff, im sorry for the trouble fierodude is no longer allowed to use the computer for his personal enjoyment, i think the rest of the forum members will be happy with this choice although if he gets his own pc , i have no control over what he does on the net<BR>so ill leave it at that<P>thanks<P>------------------<BR>it's for the better your better half is gone. It's ok you didn't need her anyway. and i don't wanna  hear you say nobody can take her place and what more kan i say you didn't need her anyways.! -less than jake<P>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6||||reg||1
Z||000013||Archie||07-03-2001||11:19 AM||||Hey Cliff, keep the forum going, it will leave a big gap in my day if you were to shut it down.<P>Just slam a few of the punks around until they either clean up their acts or leave.<P>I spend very little time in the O/T section, so, IMHO, it doesn't matter what they do over here.<P>The only reason I found this thread was a link from another thread in the Tech area.<P>BTW, would you consider either moving or shutting down this thread in the Tech section? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011760.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011760.html</A> <P>Thanks<P>Archie<P>Long live PFF.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Jaygee79||07-03-2001||11:35 AM||||I'm sorry for everything that's happened in those threads.  I don't want to see the forum shut down.  I hope it doesn't come to that.  There has to be something that can be done about this besides shutting down.  If all the members could keep their problems with other members private that would eliminate a good portion of the problem.  I don't know how feasible that is though.  Just remember, most of the people who start these threads are starting them to cause this exact thing.  They like to cause riffs between friends.  If we could just try to keep that from happening as much as possible, first of all by ignoring the remarks that these people make or by keeping it in email that would be a big help.||||reg||1
Z||000015||AkursedX||07-03-2001||12:03 PM||||I apologoze for my actions as well within that whole mess.<P>I agree with the others about how they are saying that this forum seems to have taken a turn for the worse in recent weeks.  And I have a little theory behind this.....of course the large amount of members has to do with the problems, but there is something else as well.  Cliff, correct me if I'm wrong, but isn't this site listed on a bunch of search engines now??  The way I see it, those search engines bring in lots of people, and they don't bring in the same quality of people.<P>When I joined the forum, this place was kinda like a Shangri'la, an amazing place, but very hard to find!  I think because it was like that, only real big Fiero fanactics would find this place.  I can't remember how I found the forum, but I know it wasn't through a search engine.  <P>And I really hope this place doesn't shut down, but I understand if you did do that Cliff.  Maybe you could charge a fee or something, I know I would pay to use this forum.  I practically live on here as it is anyways!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Tweek||07-03-2001||12:07 PM||||I am in agreement with Archie 100%<P>On another note... It is sooo tempting to hit the reply button when a flame war is breaking out, even if its to just say "This is stupid". But I make a point not to respond at all. <P>Cliff is a good webmaster, and its sad, but people will continue to puch his buttons, just because they can, or at least until he bans them. I suppose thats one plus for real life car clubs, not quite so anonymous.||||reg||1
Z||000017||DRH||07-03-2001||12:14 PM||||I agree with Archie. Shutting it down is a rather drastic solution. Most of the 'over the line' stuff will go away on it's on just by Cliff letting people know it's unacceptable. <P>And as Cliff pointed out, the troublemakers will get bored and leave if nobody feeds them. I know, easier said than done at times  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Voytek||07-03-2001||12:41 PM||||I've got an idea.  Let's start a new apology thread!  That way we can all tell each other what morons we were and what we shouldn't have done!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||84Bill||07-03-2001||01:10 PM||||I was not going to put up a post here but I figured ahhh who reads my stuff anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm gasping here at the events that have happened, I guess such things are going to crop up from time to time kinda like a bad car accident. <BR>I have gotten into some fairly heated battles (for me anyway) with more than one member on this forum. Even thow we disagree I consider most of them my friends. I have learned that when you look through someone else's eyes at a situation you can learn something and I have learned much on here by doing just that. I admire conviction and intelligence when in the heat of a disagreement and it gets better when you come out of it with mutual <B> respect </B> for oneanother. That's where it's at, we don't always have to agree but we must have some respect or the house will fall. <BR>2 Threads come to mind and of those two I have found much respect for several members and not because I agree with them entirely but it's because I see their point and they see mine, and I understand how important it is to them and the know likewise and at the very least we agree the Fieros are cool.<BR>So there is my penny, try not to spend it all in one (thread) place  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>I suddenly feel old, I better go post something in the Fierolisa thread quick!<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000020||saleenfiero||07-03-2001||01:12 PM||||Well if totally off-topic is becoming the waste of space that it is, then why not just kill this area?  I know us fiero folk may have similar interests, but I don't come here to discuss pointless crap and I'm sure others don't either.  That's what your friends are for.  This is a FIERO forum after all, so what's the problem with just using it as such?  Getting rid of PFF totally would just be another nail in the coffin of the fiero legacy.  This is one of the few ways we can connect around the world and it is a great time killer too!||||reg||1
Z||000021||Cliff Pennock||07-03-2001||01:17 PM||||Well, I'm a bit calmed down now. I had three hours of sleep last night and a looooooong day ahead. So when I found this crap on the forum before I had my first cup of coffee, I almost <B>did</B> shut the forum down. I still stand by what I said, however. Although I hardly have the time (my holiday starts in two weeks and I have a lot of work to do before that time), I <B>will</B> start moderating the forum from now on. I don't believe the quality of a forum like this  depends on numbers. Be it 500 members or 10000 members, if people would just treat it with the respect it IMO deserves, it will soon be the fun place it used to be again.<P>I think the cause of the downfall is indeed the O/T section. I've been letting people say whatever they damn well felt they needed to say although that was <B>never</B> the intention of the O/T section. The O/T section is for discussing other interesting stuff, stuff we might have in common, hobbies we might share, etc. It was never meant to be the "who can get the most posts in a thread about nothing at all" section.<P>So from now on I'll start closing and deleting threads. But I said it before and I'll say it again. I do not have the time to go through all the messages. So I kindly ask you to email me whenever you think a thread needs attention. I agree PFF was a much nicer place to hang around 2 years ago. But I do not agree this is forever history. I do not think closing PFF will solve anything. Another forum will pop up somewhere and will experience the same problems after time.<P>I think PFF is going through different stages. In its infancy it was nice, cute, fun and new. Right now it shows all the signs of puberty. Let's hope it will grow to adulthood very soon.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Oreif||07-03-2001||01:39 PM||||Cliff, I agree with you. Since it is impossible for you to monitor the large number of threads that get posted daily, Why don't you assign some moderators. I'm sure you could find 2 or 3 folks who don't join in the "flame wars" to moderate the threads. They would just require the ability to close a thread or delete it. They could be like "Smokey the Bear". Keeping the Flame wars to a minimum.<BR>Hopefully, we as a large group can get past the childish rantings and flame wars soon.||||reg||1
Z||000023||JohnnyK||07-03-2001||01:45 PM||||Well, as it is to be expected, I don't agree... SIgh..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I DO agree that the useless posts (such as beep, and my donut broke, etc) should be deleted as quickly as possible, but i think the ones with an actual question/statement, however offensive it might be to some should stay. I agree with the "change the channel" philosophy.. thank you||||reg||1
Z||000024||JSocha||07-03-2001||01:51 PM||||Say Cliff, have to agree with you, even if I may have been some "fuel" to the proverbial fire in certain threads.<P>My wife and I started a website called Cupids Love Connection a couple of years back.  Started out slow...then BAM!...took off like there was no tomorrow with 200+ submissions a day.<P>Our goal as well as policy was to keep it clean regarding the posts and the pictures and we listed the reasons why as we were also "publishing" a newsletter once a month of the ads that were at our website for those that did not have access to a computer.<P>Wife finally made me shut it down because not only were the submissions taking up most of my time afterwork but were becoming foul mouthed, dirty, sexually orientated and the wife was getting tired of the email submissions with nude photos to be placed with the respective ads.<P>One email attachement (wife still is unaware of it as it was purged shortly after I got it) showed one couple going at it and they were looking for someone to join in.<P>Would have made a nice ad if we were a Swingers website as they made a banner with our Cupid's Love Connection logo and hung it over their headboard.<P>Our website went from childhood innocense straight to adulthood improprieties.<P>IMO, no matter what you do here, short of shutting it down completely, you are going to experience it anyplace here at your website.  Shut down O/T, it more then likely will gradually move someplace else within the forum, start out innocent enough and just go ballistic from there.<P>I myself would hate to see your site shut down.  I am typically here morning, noon and night.  So much so, I don't even know what my wife looks like anymore.  When I meet her again, I think it will be like the first time we met...but that is another thread.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Cliff, your experiencing the internet and obviously the diverse nature of people as they come aboard.<P>No matter how somebody razzes me though, I'll let them know and/or I'll turn it into a joke, clarify my position and/or shrug my shoulders and move on with my life.<P>Noone here yet has gotten on my bad side, nor do I feel they ever will.  In the end, I feel I have made a lot of friends here and can ask for advise.  If nothing else, the O/T section has provided me a method of becoming more aquanted with people's personalities, vices, backgrounds, beliefs and where there boundaries lay.  Otherwise, in the other sections if O/T didn't exsist, they would be another nameless, electronic body devoid of any humanism/persona to relate with.<P>IMHO, I feel if I was to meet any individuals here in person, whether we were at dispute or not, I would be able to and be able to feel comfortable walking up to any person here and personally shake their hands and greet them like we hadn't seen each other in years, even when I didn't know them to begin with.  <P>The O/T section as stated, gives one an ability to put a personality with the person because they do open up more here then anyplace else on the forum and are willing to share more then they would otherwise.  And YES, some, if not all of us, do go overboard and/or get carried away.  Human nature.  Would happen if we were all to take and spend a year together at some secluded island where we would be forced to spend each and everyday being with the people in person as we do here electronically.<P>Please do not let this be a future factor if or and while Moderating the posts as a decision to remove O/T and/or shut down this forum all together.  I feel it would be more of a reactive response to the situation versus proactive.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Voytek||07-03-2001||01:56 PM||||'...it was never meant to be the 'who can get the most posts in a thread about nothing at all' section...'.<P>I was going to say something about that ealier, but chose not to.  Now that it's out in the open, here are my 3 pennies.<BR>In this case, a certain 19 page topic comes to mind.  Talk about a waste of band width.  I do agree with Cliff that O/T should still mean quality conversation about real interests or issues that affect PFF members.  Coversations about nothing belong in chat rooms and not on a FIERO forum.  Another example that comes to mind is 'sex in a Fiero'.  This thing has been beat to death by now on several occasions.  I'm sure there are 'special' forums for this type of discussion where those who need to explore their sexual frustration can do so in private.  Now, don't get me wrong.  Strange topics will come up all the time and, to a certain degree, it is OK and entertaining.  I am just using this as an example of the declining quality and 'waste-of-space' type of topics.<BR>Just my 3 cents CDN.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||AkursedX||07-03-2001||03:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Since it is impossible for you to monitor the large number of threads that get posted daily, Why don't you assign some moderators. .</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That is the best idea I have heard all day!  If you look at some of the bigger bulletin boards, they have moderators for each section, (ala LS1.com).  This way you don't have to do all the watch-dogging all by yourself.  And there are more than a few people on this forum who I think could handle that responsibility (Of course I am NOT one of them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )  <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||Standard||07-03-2001||03:07 PM||||If you don't mind volunteers, I'd be happy to moderate things for ya.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000028||DecadenceR||07-03-2001||03:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Let's hope it will grow to adulthood very soon.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>All I have to say is I totally agree.||||reg||1
Z||000029||84Bill||07-03-2001||03:14 PM||||Oreif<BR>You are in my eyes, a very respected member. However I think that disagreements "the spauners of flame wars" are what makes things interesting. IMHO it needs to be moderated with a very objective eye. I personally think Cliff had the right idea by leaving things alone. I say boot the troublmakers rather than having 1000 opinionated people sending in protest mail because they disagree with what is "realevent" to the Forum in their eyes. Because you have 1000 other that want to have that thread but will not have a reason to send an email because to them it's fine. So it's just not fair. If I had a dime for every post I saw with someone complaining about the content of a thread I'd retire right now with about three dollars and thirty cents. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I just feel that the allure of the forum is more than just Fieros and thats what I precieved O/T to be. I have other interests and inputs than just my car so O/T is valuable to me. I did not see this place from it's humbel beginings but it surly has grown.<BR>I remember AOL (yeah I hear the groans) chat rooms were great in the beginning but the same thing thappend there as here, flames errupted everywhere. They added moderators and after a while the moderators needed to be moderated. I got booted 3 times because I expressed my distaste to an ignorant bonehead that was giving a female friend a hard time. So where does it end? How does it end. <BR>I honestly don't think its bad content so much as it's bad people. If you don't like the person don't read their threads, when they come barging in a thread armed with really stupid opinions and post them. I don't even read it, I look at the name and skip it without a thought. That way I can read what I want and people can post what they want and we all can be happy to some extent. <BR>I dono where the solution is, I really would not like to be in Cliffords shoes right now. Hehe but who said being a parent to something was easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000030||Galen||07-03-2001||04:06 PM||||I guess I should apoligize for my bit too. However, I was attempting to throw a little ice on the subject.<P>Cliff, I've said it before, and I'll say it again.. YOU ARE THE MAN!<P>and AkursedX, sorry about ya keyboard and the beer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/kid.gif">         <BR>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe  <BR>AIM: GalenRPG||||reg||1
Z||000031||Monkeyman||07-03-2001||05:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>...It was never meant to be the "who can get the most posts in a thread about nothing at all" section...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cliff--I hope you aren't referring to me.  The majority of my posts haven't solved any technical problems, but I still think I've contributed to this forum.  Sometimes what people need is a laugh.  I've never been very brilliant when it comes to mechanics or electronics or computers, etc.  What I usually have to give is my humor.  It's true that sometimes I may be out of line, but it's not intentional.  This is all I have to give.  If my "5000th post" thread was out of line, I wish you had let me know.  I emailed you to let you know what I was doing (because of the large pic thing) and I didn't get much of a response anyway (so much for the kegger party!).  I've stated many times that I couldn't care less if I've posted the most or the least.  I still enjoy being part of the PFF family.  I hope you won't shut the forum down, but I'll understand if you do.  If you do decide to close the doors, would you please give us some notice so I can make sure I save some email addys, etc?<P>BTW--I sure appreciate all that you've done for us.  I don't think that a small charge would be out of line.  It might keep the instigators out.  Who wants to pay money just to aggrevate others (except my ex-wives, of course).<P><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000032||Monkeyman||07-03-2001||05:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>I remember when Monkeyman got jumped all over when he started a tabacco related thread. It seems perfectly quaint now. Any day I expect to see a thread started about setting up ones own meth lab.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Please refresh my memory.  I forget what thread you're talking about.  And are you defending me or cutting me?  I remain confusedable.<P><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000033||TRiAD||07-03-2001||05:06 PM||||Sorry for my part. I did want to see what the response was, as I was trying my best to be professional about it, but apparently it went down hill from there. <P>I hope things get better, and I hope to be a part of that. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000034||kslish||07-03-2001||06:23 PM||||I'm sure everyone will eventually cool down and more rational thoughts will prevail (hopefully).<P>It just boggles my mind that some people just don't get the concept of a forum.  Stating a thought, opinion or whatever on this forum is no different then stepping in front of an auditorium full of people with a microphone and stating how you feel.  The only difference is you won't be physically mobbed or get your @ss kicked on this forum like you would if you pissed off all those people in person. Unfortunately, this diconnection allows people to think they have balls when they really have none and they say stuff just to tick people off in general.  The only thing to do in this case is to politely ignore those individuals, because they will eventually give up if they don't get the response they were looking for. <P>I enjoy this forum because it's like a big family, a big disfunctional family sometimes though so Father (Cliff) does have to put his foot down sometimes....it's his house after all.  Can't always let the inmates run the asylum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Just my 2 cents,<P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
