Z||000040||FLASHY||07-03-2001||09:50 PM||||I for one have tried over the past week or two to avoid this forum (more so the Off Topic Section) because I found myself to be too frustrated with the BS going around lately. And until things smarten up around here I'm going to continue to keep my distance. Atleast we have a good start here. I was beginning to think this whole forum would collapse and it just about did. I was worried it was just me getting fed up with the crap but it looks like I wasn't the only one. Can we PLEASE just be normal and not try to be better or more noticed than the next guy/girl. We're all equal so lets keep it that way.<P>Thank U.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flashy_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||1
Z||000041||maryjane||07-03-2001||10:07 PM||||I heard that big communal sigh of relief all the way out here in West Texas. I belong to a couple other web organizations, mostly Military types(ex-Marine), they all have the rules posted on their opening page and all say about the same thing. Follow the rules<BR>or stay out! I'm probably older than most PFF members,(52) and have seen a lot of good things dissapear over the years because of a few peoples rudeness and bad judgment. I found this site by accident from a link and joined because I don't know much about our Fiero. It didn't take long to realize what a close knit bunch all of you are. Never met any of you but feel like I know a bunch. Cliff, YOU have done a grand thing here with this, don't blame you a bit for your actions, but remember there are a lot here that will help You anyway they can, Jane & myself included. We certainly owe that to you. Good luck and thanks.<BR>Don & Jane ||||reg||1
